{"kind":"finding","id":"F-logistics-route-021-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/Logistics/RouteHarvestAnalysisTests.cs","line":295,"method":"CollectTransportLineage_AmbiguousLineage_FallsBackLegacy_Logs","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Logistics/RouteHarvestAnalysis.cs:596; make the ambiguous branch pick the larger-overlap parent instead of returning null -> red, the opposite of the behavior the leading comment names","what_it_asserts":"CheckTransportGains returns LegacyFallback with reason ambiguous-merge-parents and logs the legacy-analysis line when two merge parents overlap the transport scope.","why_weak":"The leading comment says the test catches ambiguity being resolved by picking the larger overlap instead of degrading; production degrades (RouteHarvestAnalysis.cs:595-597) and the asserts pin degrading, so the comment misdirects a future reader.","proposed_action":"Rewrite the comment to state the fail-closed contract (ambiguous merge parents degrade to legacy, never guess a leg); optionally rename to CheckTransportGains_AmbiguousMergeParents_LegacyFallback since the test does not call CollectTransportLineage.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-logistics-route-021-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/Logistics/RouteRoundTripLinkTests.cs","line":171,"method":"Alternation_BHoldsUntilAcompletes_ThenConsumesAndHoldsAgain","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Logistics/RouteOrchestrator.cs:532; remove the LastConsumedPartnerCycle advance -> red; deleting the partner hold itself leaves every assertion here green -> green","what_it_asserts":"After two ticks both routes have CompletedCycles 1 then 2, one RouteDispatched row each per tick, and the partner cursors advanced to 0/1 then 1/2.","why_weak":"Both routes dispatch inside the same tick, so no assertion observes B holding; the name and the 'holds again' claim are pinned only by the sibling evaluator-level test.","proposed_action":"Rename to Alternation_CursorsAdvanceOnEachTick_BothConsume, and leave the hold claim to Alternation_BHoldsUntilPartnerCompletesNewCycle.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
